Inbound Traffic vs Outbound Traffic in AWS
🔹Inbound Traffic
 ☑️  Traffic that enters your AWS resources (EC2, Load Balancer, etc.)
 ☑️  Example: A user accessing your website hosted on EC2.
🔹Outbound Traffic
 ☑️ Traffic that leaves your AWS resources.
 ☑️ Example: Updating OS packages.
Inbound vs Outbound traffic helps you:
☑️ Configure security groups correctly
☑️ Manage VPC networking effectively
☑️ Control AWS data transfer costs
☑️ Improve application security
